        "prompt": "Use case: precise-object-edit. Asset type: directly sampled first-person military sleeve albedo UV patch for a realistic game. Input image is the exact edit target, a registered rectangular crop of an existing shirt atlas, NOT a photograph of a worn shirt. Rebuild this exact texture crop at substantially higher native detail. Keep the identical rectangular framing, aspect ratio 655:401, every camouflage shape boundary, cuff/placket shape, pocket edge, button, seam, insignia, padding and UV island in exactly the same normalized position. Do not rearrange or add objects. Preserve the muted tan, olive and dark brown colour palette and overall brightness. Resolve printed camo edges smoothly with sharply resolved tiny cotton yarn, restrained short twill fibres and individual small stitch loops; the cloth should look like fine realistic military cotton at arm's length rather than coarse sackcloth. Clean distinct stitching on the narrow cuff/placket at the right. The weave must be very fine, never large embossed crosshatching. Flat diffuse base-colour texture lighting, no glossy highlights, no new baked folds or shadows, no blur, no painterly strokes, no pixel grid, no sharpening halos. Keep edge colours and boundary shapes registered to the source because the material will blend this crop into the existing atlas. Output only the improved UV texture crop at the highest native landscape resolution; no labels or borders.",
